`TrieRouter` now matches a regex parameter followed by a literal bracket segment such as `/a/:id{[0-9]+}/[draft]`.

`getPattern()` in `src/utils/url.ts` was putting the next segment into the lookahead unchanged, so `[draft]` was compiled as a character class. Literal `[` and `]` are now escaped. A following `:param` or `*` is still left out of that lookahead, so regex parameters keep their own brackets.

Regression coverage:

- `TrieRouter` returns `200` with body `42` for `GET /a/42/[draft]`, `404` for `/a/42/draft` and `/a/42/[other]`, and still matches `/a/42/file.html`.
- A default `Hono` app (SmartRouter) returns `200` with body `42` for that route alone via RegExpRouter, and again after unrelated routes force a fallback to TrieRouter.

Files changed:

- `src/utils/url.ts`
- `src/utils/url.test.ts`
- `src/router/trie-router/router.test.ts`
- `src/router/smart-router/router.test.ts`

`pnpm lint` exited 0. `pnpm test` passed the router suites (RegExpRouter and LinearRouter unchanged). After a package build, the full run was 5771 passed. Four `build/jsx-types.test.ts` cases timed out at 5 seconds while spawning the TypeScript compiler against published JSX types; those are unrelated to this routing fix, so I left that harness alone.
`TrieRouter` now matches a regex parameter followed by a literal bracket segment such as `/a/:id{[0-9]+}/[draft]`.

`getPattern()` in `src/utils/url.ts` was building the next-segment lookahead without escaping brackets, so `[draft]` was compiled as a character class. Literal `[` and `]` are now escaped. A following `:param` or `*` is still left out of that lookahead, and segments without brackets (such as `file.html`) are unchanged.

**Tests**
- TrieRouter: `GET /a/42/[draft]` returns `200` / `42`; `/a/42/draft` and `/a/42/[other]` stay `404`; `/a/:id{[0-9]+}/file.html` still matches.
- SmartRouter: the same route returns `200` / `42` with only that route (`RegExpRouter`) and after extra routes force a fallback to `TrieRouter`.
- `RegExpRouter` and `LinearRouter` suites were not modified.

