`getPattern()` now escapes literal `[` and `]` in the lookahead after a regex parameter, so `TrieRouter` matches `/a/:id{[0-9]+}/[draft]` for `GET /a/42/[draft]` and returns `200` with body `42`.

A segment such as `[draft]` was inserted into the lookahead as a character class. Literal next segments are escaped (`\[draft\]`). A following `:param` or `*` is still left out of the lookahead, so those brackets stay part of the parameter pattern.

